{
  "release": "SafeGrip-Open v1.2.0 / SafeGrip-CI",
  "purpose": "risk-aware selective physics correction with strong temporal base estimator and learned correction-utility gating",
  "release_validation": {
    "pytest": "77 passed, 2 warnings",
    "python_compileall": true,
    "cli_help": true,
    "synthetic_training_smoke": true,
    "primary_ablation_count": 11,
    "supplementary_optimization_ablations": 0
  },
  "verified_invariants": [
    "full v1.2 point estimator does not recursively consume the previous predicted friction state",
    "raw sensor Conv1D+GRU temporal estimator owns the primary friction prediction",
    "counterfactual identifiability is exported and consumed as local observability evidence rather than neural-correctness authority",
    "inverse dynamics contributes only a damped trust-region-bounded residual correction",
    "physics evidence is detached before entering the point/gate path so point loss cannot improve by warping the dynamics model",
    "learned utility gate uses only inference-available evidence at inference; its oracle useful-fraction target is training-only",
    "friction-change, regime-change and asymmetric unsafe-overestimation objectives are explicit training terms",
    "no-heteroscedastic ablation removes both the heteroscedastic objective and aleatoric gate feature",
    "base-temporal ablation removes physics correction, projection-specific bound use, heteroscedastic evidence and UQ",
    "final point output respects global and enabled conditional physical support",
    "UQ remains calibrated on the disjoint UQ role with block-max split conformal calibration",
    "primary v1.2 ablation semantics are explicit and unit-tested for distinctness",
    "legacy v1.0/v1.1 proposal classes remain available only for reproducibility",
    "LiRA downloads reject zero-byte/corrupt payloads and retain public fallback behavior"
  ],
